   "text": "This is a rifamycin\u2011type ansa macrolide whose naphthoquinone core is fused to a phenoxazine bearing an (1\u2011methylpiperidin\u20113\u2011yl)methoxy substituent. I wrote the SMILES in these parts:\n\n- **Phenoxazine and piperidine:** the aryl ring carries the O\u2013CH2 link on the carbon meta to the ring oxygen. The piperidine is 3\u2011substituted and N\u2011methylated.\n- **Core:** the naphthoquinone ring has the NH\u2011bearing carbon, the ring\u2011fused phenoxazine O and N, and the ring ketone. The aromatic ring has OH and CH3, and its oxygen forms the furanone with the quaternary C(CH3), which carries the ring C=O.\n- **Ansa chain:** from the amide the chain runs C(=O)\u2013C(CH3)=CH\u2013CH=CH\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OAc)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OMe)\u2013CH=CH\u2013O back to the quaternary carbon.\n\nI did not derive the stereocentres independently from the wedges and hashes. I took the chain and quaternary\u2011centre stereochemistry from the standard rifamycin/rifampicin configuration as I remember it, and kept the neighbour order around the quaternary carbon the same so the chirality tags carry over. I assumed the drawing matches that natural configuration, but I did not check each centre against the image. I checked the ring\u2011closure digits for consistency and the 3\u2011substitution of the piperidine against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1/C=C/C=C(\\C(=O)NC2=C3Oc4cc(OCC5CCCN(C)C5)ccc4N=C3C6=C(C(=O)[C@](O7)(O/C=C/[C@@H]([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]1O)C)O)C)OC(=O)C)C)OC)C)C7=C(C)C(O)=C6C2=O)/C"
